[R3 DESIGN NOTE - LAW-SHAPE ANALYSIS; READ BEFORE BUILDING R4] The handoff's literal
slot-free claim "(dbar (pouSplit ∘ (chart j).symm))_j ∈ oneOneCoeff" is NOT provable over
the landed R2 interface, and is false for nontrivial data: R2's w is SCALAR overlap data
(plain additive IsOverlapCocycle - the ML m_j - m_i shape; a form-coefficient family
cannot satisfy the plain additive triple-overlap identity across charts), so the
telescope forces s_k∘φ - s_j = (holomorphic), pinning the transformation of ∂̄s to the
(0,1) factor conj φ' ALONE.  A family obeying both the (0,1) and the (1,1) law would
need φ' ≡ 1 wherever it is nonzero.  R1's OneOneLawAt was NOT adjusted - it is correct
as landed (normSq φ' is what Lebesgue change-of-variables patches in R4).  The factors
reconcile exactly as the handoff's NOTE says: the second φ' enters via the holomorphic
change of the dz-slot, which on scalar overlap data must be an explicit input - the
holomorphic (1,0) chart-coefficient family IsOneZeroCoeff g (overlap law
g_j = (g_k ∘ φ)·φ', i.e. the chart coefficients of a global holomorphic 1-form; in the
residue application, of the S1 canonical form ω₀ with K = div ω₀).  Headline family:
t_j := dbar(s_j)·g_j  =  the chart coefficient of Forster's τ = ∂̄(σ_scalar·ω₀).
APPLICATION CONSTRAINT recorded for R4/R6: at K = div ω₀ ≠ 0 (genus ≥ 2) the scalar
Z¹(O_K) data has poles at K-points, so HolomorphicOnOverlaps requires the chart-disk
cover REFINED so each of the finitely many K-points lies in a single cover set (then
w k j is holomorphic on every overlap, and at a K-point of U_j only the k = j term of
σ_j survives, killed by the cocycle diagonal w j j = 0).  Genus 1: K = 0, no refinement.
The ω₀-witness for IsOneZeroCoeff is a later lane-R rung (germ-extraction layer).

